{
  "version": "1.0",
  "name": "Tutorial 5: Learning to Count",
  "description": "LSTM can count pulses over long sequences!\n\nUNLIKE the simple RNN which forgets after ~10 steps,\nLSTM has a CELL STATE that acts as long-term memory.\n\nTHE LSTM GATES:\n- Forget Gate: What to erase from memory\n- Input Gate: What new info to store\n- Output Gate: What to output from memory\n\nThese gates let LSTM decide what to remember and what to forget.\n\nTRY THIS:\n1. Click the Pulse button to send a 1.0\n2. Watch the counter increment\n3. Keep clicking - LSTM keeps counting!\n4. Reset states to start over\n\nThis is how LSTMs can track things over hundreds of steps -\nthe cell state maintains information the gates decide to keep.\n\nReal-world use: This is how language models remember context\nacross long documents.",
  "metadata": {
    "created": "2025-12-19T20:50:00",
    "modified": "2025-12-19T20:50:00",
