    {
      "id": "comment-0e6a8e26-ea88-4bb3-bbd7-bea5e2924344",
      "type": "COMMENT",
      "name": "Welcome",
      "position": [
        50,
        50
      ],
      "params": {
        "text": "# Counting Network - Learning to Count\n\nCan a neural network learn to count? Let's find out!\n\n## To Do and Notice\n\n1. **Sequence processing**: How does the network handle different length inputs?\n2. **State accumulation**: Watch the hidden state grow with each input\n3. **The output**: Does it accurately count?\n\n## Why Counting is Hard\n\nCounting seems simple but requires:\n- Memory (how many so far?)\n- Increment operation\n- Generalization to unseen lengths\n\n**Challenge**: What's the maximum count this network can handle accurately?",
        "width": 450,
        "show_on_start": true
      },
      "inputs": {},
      "outputs": {},
      "weights": {},
      "collapsed": false,
      "color": "#5c4a3d",
      "tags": [],
      "description": "Tutorial introduction"
    }
